    <!-- 06 Content Formats That Drive Sales -->
    <section class="guide-section" id="content-formats">
      <div class="max-w-[800px] mx-auto px-6">
        <div class="font-mono text-[11px] font-medium uppercase tracking-[.1em] text-accent mb-2">06 &mdash; Content Formats</div>
        <h2 class="font-display font-bold text-[clamp(24px,3.5vw,32px)] leading-[1.15] tracking-[-0.02em] text-ink mb-2">Content formats that drive sales</h2>
        <div class="tldr">
          <ul class="list-none p-0 m-0 space-y-1">
            <li class="text-[14px] text-ink-2 before:content-['—_'] before:text-accent before:font-semibold">"Get ready with me" and routine videos convert best for beauty and fashion</li>
            <li class="text-[14px] text-ink-2 before:content-['—_'] before:text-accent before:font-semibold">Unboxing and first-impression videos drive impulse purchases</li>
            <li class="text-[14px] text-ink-2 before:content-['—_'] before:text-accent before:font-semibold">Comparison and "honest review" formats build trust for higher-priced items</li>
          </ul>
        </div>
        <p class="text-ink-2 leading-[1.65] mb-4">Not all content formats convert equally on TikTok Shop. Based on performance data across thousands of shoppable videos, certain structures consistently outperform. The "get ready with me" (GRWM) format works exceptionally well for beauty and fashion &mdash; the creator walks through a routine while naturally incorporating 2&ndash;4 tagged products. Viewers watch the full routine (high retention) and buy the products that caught their attention. GRWM videos average 3&ndash;5x higher conversion rates than simple product showcases.</p>
        <p class="text-ink-2 leading-[1.65] mb-4">Unboxing and first-impression videos drive impulse purchases. The format creates a sense of discovery &mdash; the viewer experiences the product reveal alongside the creator, which triggers the "I want that too" response. These videos work best for products with strong visual appeal or satisfying packaging. Keep unboxings under 45 seconds and lead with the reaction shot, not the box.</p>
        <p class="text-ink-2 leading-[1.65] mb-4">For higher-priced items ($50+), comparison and "honest review" formats build the trust necessary for considered purchases. A creator comparing two similar products and explaining why they prefer one over the other gives the viewer the decision-making framework they need. The key is credibility: the creator must acknowledge trade-offs and downsides. "It is not perfect &mdash; the battery only lasts 6 hours &mdash; but for the price, nothing else comes close" converts better than unqualified praise.</p>
        <p class="text-ink-2 leading-[1.65] mb-4">TikTok LIVE shopping is an underused format that deserves attention. Creators go live, demonstrate products in real time, answer viewer questions, and offer time-limited discounts. LIVE sessions with product pins generate 5&ndash;10x the GMV per viewer of standard shoppable videos because the interactive format creates urgency. Brands that combine regular shoppable UGC with weekly LIVE sessions see 40&ndash;60% higher total GMV than those running short-form video alone. For guidance on how to boost top-performing videos with paid budget, see our <a href="/spark-ads" class="text-accent hover:underline">Spark Ads guide</a>.</p>
        <p class="text-ink-2 leading-[1.65] mb-4">The "problem &rarr; solution" format remains the highest-converting structure across all product categories. The creator identifies a specific, relatable frustration in the first 3 seconds ("My kitchen counter was always cluttered and I could not find anything"), then introduces the product as the solution ("until I found this $22 organizer"). This format works because it mirrors how people actually discover products in real life &mdash; through a need, not through an ad. Keep the problem specific and the solution visual. Abstract pain points ("I wanted to be more organized") convert far worse than concrete ones ("I kept losing my keys every morning").</p>
        <p class="text-ink-2 leading-[1.65] mb-4">Seasonal and trend-based content provides short bursts of high performance. Tie your TikTok Shop UGC to trending sounds, seasonal events (back to school, holiday gifting, summer essentials), or platform trends. A product video using a trending sound can see 3&ndash;5x the organic reach of the same content without the trend hook. The trade-off is a shorter content shelf life &mdash; trend-based videos peak within 48&ndash;72 hours, so you need to produce and publish them quickly. Have 2&ndash;3 creators on standby for rapid-response trend content.</p>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- 07 Measuring Performance -->
    <section class="guide-section" id="measuring-performance">
      <div class="max-w-[800px] mx-auto px-6">
        <div class="font-mono text-[11px] font-medium uppercase tracking-[.1em] text-accent mb-2">07 &mdash; Performance</div>
        <h2 class="font-display font-bold text-[clamp(24px,3.5vw,32px)] leading-[1.15] tracking-[-0.02em] text-ink mb-2">Measuring TikTok Shop UGC performance</h2>
        <div class="tldr">
          <ul class="list-none p-0 m-0 space-y-1">
            <li class="text-[14px] text-ink-2 before:content-['—_'] before:text-accent before:font-semibold">GMV per video is the primary metric, not views or engagement</li>
            <li class="text-[14px] text-ink-2 before:content-['—_'] before:text-accent before:font-semibold">Track video-to-purchase conversion rate to compare creator effectiveness</li>
            <li class="text-[14px] text-ink-2 before:content-['—_'] before:text-accent before:font-semibold">Commission cost as percentage of GMV determines program profitability</li>
          </ul>
        </div>
        <p class="text-ink-2 leading-[1.65] mb-4">TikTok Shop gives brands something most social commerce channels do not: closed-loop attribution. Every sale is tracked from video view to checkout, with clear data on which creator, which video, and which product drove the transaction. This makes measurement straightforward, but it also requires shifting your KPI framework from engagement metrics to commerce metrics.</p>
        <p class="text-ink-2 leading-[1.65] mb-4">GMV (gross merchandise value) per video is the single most important metric. A video that generates $2,000 in sales from 50,000 views is worth more than a video with 500,000 views and $200 in sales. Calculate GMV per video for every piece of content and rank creators accordingly. Over time, this ranking reveals which creators consistently drive revenue and which produce content that entertains but does not convert.</p>
        <p class="text-ink-2 leading-[1.65] mb-4">Video-to-purchase conversion rate (purchases / video views) lets you compare content effectiveness independently of reach. A 0.5% conversion rate is average for TikTok Shop content; anything above 1% is strong; above 2% is exceptional. Track this metric at both the video level and the creator level to identify patterns. Some creators consistently hit 1.5%+ conversion rates regardless of the product &mdash; those are the ones to retain on commissioned contracts.</p>
        <p class="text-ink-2 leading-[1.65] mb-4">For affiliate programs, total commission paid as a percentage of GMV is your profitability metric. If you offer 15% commission and your average order value is $40, you are paying $6 per order in creator costs. Compare this to your customer acquisition cost on other channels. Most brands find that TikTok Shop affiliate costs run 30&ndash;50% lower than Meta or Google acquisition costs, making the channel highly efficient when you factor in the content production benefit &mdash; you get both the sale and the content asset.</p>

        <h3 class="font-display font-semibold text-[20px] tracking-[-0.01em] mt-8 mb-3">Key metrics at a glance</h3>
        <div class="overflow-x-auto rounded-xl border border-border bg-card mb-6">
          <table class="w-full border-collapse text-[14px]">
