        <p class="text-ink-2 leading-[1.65] mb-4">One underrated metric is content velocity &mdash; how many new shoppable videos you publish per week. TikTok Shop's algorithm rewards consistent publishing with higher placement in the Shop tab and product search results. Brands that publish fewer than 5 shoppable videos per week often see their Shop tab traffic plateau. Aim for 10+ new videos per week to maintain momentum, which typically requires a roster of 15&ndash;25 active creators.</p>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- 08 Scaling TikTok Shop Content -->
    <section class="guide-section" id="scaling">
      <div class="max-w-[800px] mx-auto px-6">
        <div class="font-mono text-[11px] font-medium uppercase tracking-[.1em] text-accent mb-2">08 &mdash; Scaling</div>
        <h2 class="font-display font-bold text-[clamp(24px,3.5vw,32px)] leading-[1.15] tracking-[-0.02em] text-ink mb-2">Scaling TikTok Shop content</h2>
        <div class="tldr">
          <ul class="list-none p-0 m-0 space-y-1">
            <li class="text-[14px] text-ink-2 before:content-['—_'] before:text-accent before:font-semibold">Start with 5&ndash;10 creators and scale to 50+ once you identify winning formats</li>
            <li class="text-[14px] text-ink-2 before:content-['—_'] before:text-accent before:font-semibold">Systematize briefs, shipping, and QA to avoid bottlenecks</li>
            <li class="text-[14px] text-ink-2 before:content-['—_'] before:text-accent before:font-semibold">Repurpose top TikTok Shop content across <a href="/ugc-for-brands" class="text-accent hover:underline">other UGC channels</a></li>
          </ul>
        </div>
        <p class="text-ink-2 leading-[1.65] mb-4">Scaling TikTok Shop UGC is a logistics challenge more than a creative one. The first bottleneck is product samples: every commissioned creator needs the product in hand before filming, and every affiliate needs access to purchase or receive a sample. Set up a dedicated sample fulfillment pipeline &mdash; pre-pack sample kits, use a shipping service that provides tracking, and send samples in batches rather than one-off. Brands that scale past 20 creators without a sample system inevitably hit delays that stall content production for weeks.</p>
        <p class="text-ink-2 leading-[1.65] mb-4">The second bottleneck is briefing. As your creator roster grows, you cannot brief each creator individually over DMs. Build a standardized brief template that covers product positioning, key claims, required CTAs, visual guidelines, and compliance restrictions. Share briefs through a centralized system &mdash; a shared Google Doc, Notion page, or project management tool. The brief should be specific enough to ensure brand consistency but flexible enough to let each creator bring their authentic voice. A rigid script defeats the purpose of UGC.</p>
        <p class="text-ink-2 leading-[1.65] mb-4">Quality assurance is the third bottleneck. At 10 videos per week, you can review each one manually. At 50+ videos per week, you need a QA process. OKAD runs a tiered review system: first-pass QA checks compliance (product tags present, claims accurate, no competitor mentions), second-pass reviews content quality (hook strength, demo clarity, audio quality). Videos that pass both go live. Videos that fail get specific revision notes &mdash; never vague feedback like "make it better," always actionable direction like "reshoot the demo under natural light and mention the price before the CTA."</p>
        <p class="text-ink-2 leading-[1.65] mb-4">Once you have a library of high-performing TikTok Shop videos, repurpose them. Top converters can be promoted as <a href="/spark-ads" class="text-accent hover:underline">Spark Ads</a>, re-edited for Instagram Reels or YouTube Shorts, or used as raw material for <a href="/ugc-for-brands" class="text-accent hover:underline">cross-platform UGC campaigns</a>. The content you produce for TikTok Shop is not single-use &mdash; it is the foundation of a multi-channel content engine. Brands working with OKAD typically see 10,000+ pieces of content delivered across all platforms from a single production pipeline.</p>
        <p class="text-ink-2 leading-[1.65] mb-4">The final piece of the scaling puzzle is creator retention. Your top-performing creators &mdash; the ones consistently hitting 1%+ conversion rates &mdash; are your most valuable assets. Move them from one-off commissions to recurring contracts with guaranteed monthly volume. Offer higher commission tiers, priority access to new product launches, and performance bonuses tied to GMV milestones. A creator who generates $10,000+ in monthly GMV is worth investing in &mdash; losing them to a competitor costs far more than a modest rate increase.</p>

